--TEST--
Core\IO::stat answers in one call what ::size, ::isFile, ::isDir and ::modifiedAt answer in four, and every pair agrees — asserted by counting the agreements rather than by printing each answer, so a member that grew its own reading of the same `stat` fails here while still looking right on its own line — spec § 14, `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R17
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The four single-question members and the one that answers all four exist
// side by side on purpose: this case is the rule that makes that legal. They
// are not two spellings of one operation -- each static reaches the operating
// system with a path, while each member of the snapshot reads a slot -- but
// they must never disagree about a file nothing is writing.
Core\IO::write("note.txt", "hello world\n");
Core\IO::makeDir("sub");

var $file = Core\IO::stat("note.txt");
var $dir = Core\IO::stat("sub");

// Counted, not read off a line. Four agreements is the whole assertion; a
// member answering plausibly on its own row still fails this.
int $agree = 0;

if (($file->size() as int) == (Core\IO::size("note.txt") as int)) {
    $agree = $agree + 1;
}
if ($file->isFile() == Core\IO::isFile("note.txt")) {
    $agree = $agree + 1;
}
if ($file->isDir() == Core\IO::isDir("note.txt")) {
    $agree = $agree + 1;
}
// The modification time is a point on the timeline and not a number, so the
// comparison is `compareTo` -- `rule:core-api/shape-rules` R12's units-are-types, and the whole
// reason `filemtime`'s epoch integer does not survive into Novis.
if ($file->modifiedAt()->compareTo(Core\IO::modifiedAt("note.txt")) == 0) {
    $agree = $agree + 1;
}

echo "agreeing answers: ", $agree as string, "\n";

// And the same four questions of a directory, where two of them swap. The
// pair partitions most of what exists without covering it, which is
// `isFile`/`isDir`'s own rule stated over a snapshot instead of over a path.
if ($dir->isDir() == Core\IO::isDir("sub")) {
    echo "directory: isDir agrees\n";
}
if ($dir->isFile() == Core\IO::isFile("sub")) {
    echo "directory: isFile agrees\n";
}
if ($file->isFile()) {
    echo "note.txt: a file\n";
}
if ($dir->isDir()) {
    echo "sub: a directory\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
write = ["."]
--EXPECT--
agreeing answers: 4
directory: isDir agrees
directory: isFile agrees
note.txt: a file
sub: a directory
